==Trivia==
*Her [[Sinner Snache]]-like tail is a reference to the canine guardian of the underworld in Greek Mythology, [[wikipedia:Cerberus|Cerberus]], who is commonly depicted with a serpent for a tail.
*In her Japanese name, Deviru Fujin (デヴィル夫人, "Lady Devil"), "Devil" is transliterated as デヴィル ''Deviru'' rather than デビル ''Debiru'' like in the names of other [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] enemies such as [[Aku Doge]] and [[Aku Cyclone]]. This is most likely a pun on Devi Fujin (デヴィ夫人, "Lady Dewi"), a nickname for Japanese-born Indonesian businesswoman, socialite, TV personality and philanthropist [[wikipedia:Dewi Sukarno|Dewi Sukarno]]. Like Devil Wife, Dewi has made many donations to the less fortunate.
*"Famous for making waves with her fashion" refers to her [[Death Surge]] ability, whose Japanese name (デス烈波 ''Desu Reppa'') translates to "Death Intense Wave".
*She is the only non-[[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]] enemy to have debuted in a Colossus [[Gauntlet]].
*In [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]], Devil Wife was introduced in [[Attack of the Omens]], but her first appearance in all other versions was in [[Muddy Fjord]], as Attack of the Omens was not released outside of Japan until May 22nd, 2023, while [[Cats Cradle Basin]] was made available worldwide on May 17th.

